FEX-Emu
-------
https://github.com/FEX-Emu/FEX (reference checkout: commit ea43314f040633c76fb5891ff31d8a7c3dc533b8)

Used as the semantic reference for several x86 lowerings in pkg/lifter and pkg/disasm. No FEX
source file is included; the lowerings are written for this lifter and cite the FEX function
they follow in their comments:

  - lazy PF/AF (pkg/lifter/arm64_lifter_parity.go, pkg/disasm/parity.go):
    FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Flags.cpp (CalculatePF, CalculateAF,
    LoadPFRaw, LoadAF, ZeroPF_AF)
  - DF and backward string instructions, LAHF/SAHF, PUSHFQ/POPFQ:
    FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp (FLAGControlOp, SAHFOp, LAHFOp, PUSHFOp,
    POPFOp, the string operations) and OpcodeDispatcher.h (ForeachDirection)
  - FCOMI/FCOMIP/FUCOMI/FUCOMIP and the x87 constant loads:
    FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp (FCOMI, FLD_Const),
    FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/X86Tables/X87Tables.cpp
  - MMX PSHUFW: FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp (PSHUFW8ByteOp)

Test cases in pkg/lifter/arm64_fex_cases_test.go (generated by tools/gen_fex_cases.py) restate
unit tests from FEX's unittests/ASM directory: their instruction sequences and expected
register values (RegData).

The instruction-level differential suite (cmd/fexasm, tools/fex_oracle.sh,
docs/m1/fex-oracle.md) uses FEX's unittests/ASM corpus as test input and expected-result
oracle. Those tests are not vendored: they are read from a local clone, assembled with nasm
and lifted; no x86 code is executed.

